<section class="tb-seo">
  <div class="tb-seo-inner">
    <h2>Custom Embroidered Hats, Made in Burlington, North Carolina</h2>
    <p>Threadbreak is a custom embroidery shop based in Burlington, North Carolina, specializing in custom embroidered hats for businesses, brands, teams, and events. Every order is digitized, embroidered, inspected, and shipped from our own shop, so you get consistent, high-quality results without the middleman. Whether you need five hats or a few hundred, we make it easy to put your logo on a cap you will actually want to wear.</p>
    <h3>Popular Hat Styles</h3>
    <p>We carry a curated lineup of the most popular blank hats in the industry, including structured trucker caps, flat-bill snapbacks, rope hats, five-panel and seven-panel styles, and premium performance caps. Popular options include the Richardson 112, Richardson 168 seven-panel, Richardson 256 Umpqua rope hat, Yupoong retro truckers, Otto five-panel caps, and more. Each style is available in a wide range of colors, so you can match your brand exactly.</p>
    <h3>Pricing &amp; Included Services</h3>
    <p>Our minimum order is 5 hats. For businesses ordering custom hats in bulk, the per-hat price drops as your quantity grows, with wholesale pricing beginning at 10 hats. We digitize your logo for embroidery at no extra charge, and shipping is always free to the lower 48. For businesses and organizations, our wholesale pricing on larger runs makes branded headwear an affordable, professional way to promote your company, outfit your team, or hand out merchandise at events.</p>
    <h3>Other Decoration Options</h3>
    <p>Beyond embroidery, we also offer laser-engraved leatherette patch hats for a premium, textured look, along with DTG printing for apparel. Have a question before you order, or need a rush? Reach out to <a href="mailto:help@threadbreak.com">help@threadbreak.com</a> and we will help you get exactly what you need. Ready to get started? <a href="/pages/custom-order">Place a custom order</a> or <a href="/pages/quote">request a quote</a> today.</p>
  </div>
</section>
